no concurrent sequence of method calls can lead to race conditions.
---Mandatory---
1. Execute the program several times. Show the results you get. Are there any race conditions?

Yes!
Sum is 1105101.000000 and should be 2000000.000000
Thus a race condition is present.

2. Explain why race conditions appear when t1 and t2 use the Mystery object. Hint: Consider (a) what it
means for an instance method to be synchronized, and (b) what it means for a static method to be synchronized.

They use two different locks.

1. Intrinsic lock on the instance: public synchronized void addInstance(double x)
    //this is equivalent to locking Mystery m = new Mystery();
2. Intrinsic lock on the class: public static synchronized void addStatic(double x)
    //This is equivalent to locking Mystery.class
When the first lock is acquired, the second lock can still be acquired by another thread.
Thus the sum can be updated by two threads at the same time.


